    "question_text": "4. What were the major ideas expressed by Kabir? How did he express these?",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "The major ideas expressed by Kabir: (i) His teachings were based on a complete, indeed vehement, rejection of the major religious traditions. (ii) He openly ridiculed all forms of external worship of both Brahmanical Hinduism and Islam. (iii) He believed in a formless Supreme God. (iv) He preached that the only path to salvation was through bhakti or devotion. He expressed these by the language of his poetry, which was a form of spoken Hindi widely understood by ordinary people.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, Kabir's teachings emphasized devotion and a personal connection to the divine, transcending traditional religious boundaries.",
    "answer_image": {
      "present": false,
