    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "6. Why do you think many teachers rejected prevalent religious beliefs and practices?",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "(i) Many teachers rejected prevalent religious beliefs and practices because it created differences in the society. (ii) Those teachings favoured the upper caste people and lower caste people suffered. (iii) The idea that all human beings are not equal were prevailing in the society and must be abolished. (iv) They believed in equality of God and want to break the evils of the society. (v) Bondage can be broken if approached God with devotion.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, the rejection of prevalent beliefs was rooted in a desire for social equality and spiritual integrity.",
